.Dd $Mdocdate: {{mdocdate}} $
.Dt {{daemon_name | upcase}}.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm {{daemon_name}}.conf
.Nd {{daemon_name}} configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr {{daemon_name}} 8
reads its configuration from
.Pa /etc/{{daemon_name}}.conf ,
or the file given with
.Fl f .
A missing default file is treated as empty; a missing file given with
.Fl f
is an error.
The file is TOML.
Unknown keys are rejected.
All keys are optional.
.Sh SETTINGS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm socket No = Ar path
Control socket, overridden by
.Fl s .
Must be absolute.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/{{daemon_name}}.sock .
.It Cm user No = Ar string
Run the engine process as this user.
.Xr {{daemon_name}} 8
must then be started as root.
Default: unset, run as the invoking user.
.It Cm chroot No = Ar path
Directory the engine is confined to with
.Xr chroot 2
when
.Cm user
is set.
Must be absolute, owned by root and not writable by group or others.
Default: the home directory of
.Cm user .
.It Cm interval No = Ar integer
Seconds between runs of the periodic task.
Must be at least 1.
Default: 60.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/{{daemon_name}}.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/{{daemon_name}}.conf
Default location.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
socket = "/var/run/{{daemon_name}}.sock"
user = "_{{crate_name}}"
chroot = "/var/empty"
interval = 30
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr {{daemon_name}} 8 ,
.Xr {{ctl_name}} 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An {{author_name}} Aq Mt {{author_email}}
